From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emir Beganovic <beganovic.emir@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:57:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rtc: pm8xxx: honour the time zone in the UEFI offset

The RTCInfo UEFI variable that holds the offset is shared with the
firmware and Windows, and they keep that offset in local time: the two
bytes after it are the EFI_TIME TimeZone it was set for, in minutes,
with Localtime = UTC - TimeZone, followed by the EFI_TIME Daylight byte.
The driver ignores both and treats the local time as UTC.

On an ASUS Zenbook 14 UX3480QA the variable reads

	ac 61 07 58 20 fe 01 00 00 00 00 00

that is a TimeZone of -480 (UTC+8) and Daylight 0x01
(EFI_TIME_ADJUST_DAYLIGHT). Windows, set to W. Europe Standard Time,
showed the right time, while Linux set the system clock exactly 28800
seconds ahead at boot. When NTP then set the RTC, the driver stored a
UTC offset next to the unchanged -480, which the firmware and Windows
read as 8 hours behind.

Add the time zone when reading the offset and subtract it when writing,
leaving it untouched. An unspecified (0x7ff) or out-of-range time zone
keeps the current behaviour.

Fixes: bba38b874886 ("rtc: pm8xxx: add support for uefi offset")
Signed-off-by: Emir Beganovic <beganovic.emir@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/rtc/rtc-pm8xxx.c | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/rtc/rtc-pm8xxx.c b/drivers/rtc/rtc-pm8xxx.c
index e624f84..7897c9d 100644
--- a/drivers/rtc/rtc-pm8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/rtc/rtc-pm8xxx.c
@@ -50,7 +50,9 @@ struct pm8xxx_rtc_regs {
 
 struct qcom_uefi_rtc_info {
 	__le32	offset_gps;
-	u8	reserved[8];
+	__le16	timezone;
+	u8	daylight;
+	u8	reserved[5];
 } __packed;
 
 /**
@@ -92,6 +94,21 @@ MODULE_IMPORT_NS("EFIVAR");
 			 EFI_VARIABLE_BOOTSERVICE_ACCESS | \
 			 EFI_VARIABLE_RUNTIME_ACCESS)
 
+/*
+ * The firmware keeps the offset in local time, with the time zone it was set
+ * for stored next to it as in EFI_TIME, where Localtime = UTC - TimeZone (in
+ * minutes). Return the seconds to add to that local time to get UTC.
+ */
+static s32 pm8xxx_rtc_uefi_tz_secs(const struct qcom_uefi_rtc_info *rtc_info)
+{
+	s16 tz = (s16)le16_to_cpu(rtc_info->timezone);
+
+	if (tz == EFI_UNSPECIFIED_TIMEZONE || tz < -1440 || tz > 1440)
+		return 0;
+
+	return tz * 60;
+}
+
 static int pm8xxx_rtc_read_uefi_offset(struct pm8xxx_rtc *rtc_dd)
 {
 	struct qcom_uefi_rtc_info *rtc_info = &rtc_dd->rtc_info;
@@ -121,9 +138,10 @@ static int pm8xxx_rtc_read_uefi_offset(struct pm8xxx_rtc *rtc_dd)
 
 	dev_dbg(dev, "uefi_rtc_info = %*ph\n", (int)size, rtc_info);
 
-	/* Convert from GPS to Unix time offset */
+	/* Convert from GPS local time to Unix time (UTC) offset */
 	offset_gps = le32_to_cpu(rtc_info->offset_gps);
-	rtc_dd->offset = offset_gps + (u32)RTC_TIMESTAMP_EPOCH_GPS;
+	rtc_dd->offset = offset_gps + (u32)RTC_TIMESTAMP_EPOCH_GPS +
+			 pm8xxx_rtc_uefi_tz_secs(rtc_info);
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -136,8 +154,9 @@ static int pm8xxx_rtc_write_uefi_offset(struct pm8xxx_rtc *rtc_dd, u32 offset)
 	efi_status_t status;
 	u32 offset_gps;
 
-	/* Convert from Unix to GPS time offset */
-	offset_gps = offset - (u32)RTC_TIMESTAMP_EPOCH_GPS;
+	/* Convert from Unix time (UTC) to GPS local time offset */
+	offset_gps = offset - (u32)RTC_TIMESTAMP_EPOCH_GPS -
+		     pm8xxx_rtc_uefi_tz_secs(rtc_info);
 
 	rtc_info->offset_gps = cpu_to_le32(offset_gps);
 
-- 
